Package: LeafInjuryR
Type: Package
Title: Quantification of Visual Leaf Injury Patterns from Digital
        Images
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Wilhan Valasco",
    family = "dos Santos",
    email = "wilhanvalasco@hotmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")
    )
Description: Classical image-processing pipeline to quantify visual injury
    patterns on detached leaves photographed against a contrasting background.
    The pipeline separates three steps: (1) leaf/background segmentation,
    (2) classification of leaf tissue (healthy/injured, or optionally
    healthy/chlorotic/necrotic/other) using only pixels inside the leaf mask,
    and (3) quantification of injured area as a percentage of leaf area.
    Six public functions cover cropping, automatic and manually corrected
    segmentation, single and batch analysis, validation against manually
    produced reference masks (IoU, Dice, sensitivity, specificity, precision,
    F1) and a local 'shiny' interface. Batch analyses produce a
    self-contained HTML report, an Excel workbook and a CSV table from the
    same results, with full parameter records for reproducibility. The package quantifies
    visual patterns only; it does not diagnose pathogens, diseases,
    nutritional disorders or phytotoxicity. All processing is local.
